 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Part three. Kit runs across the street with *two identical keys*.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Ruth opens the door only after he says the rules out loud.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "She sits him down and tells him about the man who lived in his house.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "In 2009, he fed the black dog *by hand*, like a pet.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "After that, the dog stopped eating from bowls.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "It didn't want food anymore. It wanted to be *invited in*.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "The man opened his door one night. They never found him.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Stay, because the dog had already chosen Kit's door.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "That night Kit locks every window and sits facing the front door.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "At 3 AM, three soft knocks.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then his father's voice: Kit, it's cold, let me in.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "His father lives two thousand miles away.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "The knocking goes on until sunrise. Kit never opens.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "In the morning, the street is quiet. Too quiet.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Ruth's front door is wide open. Her house is *empty*.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "On his own porch there's a metal bowl, licked clean.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "It's Ruth's bowl. Her name is written on the bottom.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "On Alder Street, there's a new rule now: count your neighbors.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
